    <DataNode elementId="AT5G23020-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G23020-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT5G23020-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">2-isopropylmalate synthase is the first committed enzyme in leucine biosynthesis. It is the branch point of leucine biosynthesis and the other two branched chain amino acid biosynthesis. The enzyme is feedback inhibited by the end product leucine. The Arabidopsis genome contains four highly homologous genes coding for 2-isopropylmalate synthase. Two of them, IMS2 (AT5G23020) and IMS3 (AT5G23010) have been shown to functionally complement an &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; mutant strain of 2-isopropylmalate synthase. IMS1 (AT1G74040), IMS2 and IMS3 have overlapping yet distinct expression patterns. IMS1 is expressed at low levels in roots, leaves, stems and flowers. IMS2 is expressed at high levels in roots, leaves and stems, but low levels in flowers. IMS3 is also expressed at high levels in roots, leaves and stems but is absent in flowers. The enzymes have not been purified or biochemically characterized.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G23020-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33948, RXN-33947, RXN-17747, RXN-9637, RXN-9636, RXN-9635, RXN-9634, RXN-9633, RXN-9632" />
